I finally finished the last role I had remaining, so I've now ascended
one of all 13 roles (I did a couple more than once, so it's not
actually my 13th ascension in total).  It also marks the first time
I've ascended back-to-back characters--I had done 2 out of 3 before.
(this streak is already over at 2).

Of special note in this game was the absence of any sort of magic
resistance or reflection before (or at) Medusa.  On DL1 I'd found a
/polymorph, 2 zaps had turned my little dog into a red dragon--a
jackpot that made the early game pretty trivial (mines, sokoban, etc).

A few levels past Sokoban I had found a couple huge barracks, I was
able to stay out of LOF of potential death wands while Flamer wiped out
the soldiers.  But no goodies.  In the second barracks, the dragon
passed on to the next world.  I tamed a dog and headed back to a
polytrap in the Mines, hoping for a gray/silver dragon, but stopped
when I wound up w/ a titan.

Having not yet attempted the Quest, I crossed Medusa by jumping hoping
to find reflection.  Put on a blindfold and whacked at Medusa, who fled
downstairs; before pursuing I blasted the statues with /striking, but
there was nothing useful there.

Heading downstairs, Medusa teleported away--and telepathy showed a
golden naga who I didn't want to run into just yet.

Well, I had a blessed magic lamp from Minetown.  I decided it was worth
burning it to get reflection to get me to the Castle.  Unfortunately,
the djinni I freed vanished with merely a thanks.

So I headed upstairs (titan in tow) and considered my options:

1. Do the quest to get levitation, try to avoid the naga, and see if
the Castle dragons could provide me with anything.
2. Polypile--I'd found 2 amulets, numerous elven cloaks/boots, and a
couple /polymorph
3. Use the front gate of the castle to wipe out the denizens and go for
the wand.
4. Altar camp hoping for Magicbane
5. There was 1 throne I hadn't exhausted yet.

Everything else (quaffing fountains, etc) seemed pretty high-risk and
low reward.

First, the throne.  No luck there--it did give me a genocide, and I
decided on black dragons both to eliminate a potential instadeath and
to increase my odds of useful scales at the Castle.

I decided to polypile next.  I gathered up every piece of magical armor
I could find, carefully built some piles of them and my amulets, and
luck was on my side--I got "reflection and an =levitation.

I was more comfortable descending with reflection, though the naga
still worried me--I had a scroll of genocide but wanted to elminate any
teleporting liches at the Castle.  Thankfully my titan wiped out the
naga--and then I stupidly forgot to keep it away from Medusa and it
became a statue.  Ah, well, at least I could proceed.

Descending to the castle, telepathy turned up a gray dragon.  I floated
around back after stoning the eels to death, and luck was finally on my
side--it dropped scales, and I had 1 scroll of enchant armor.

The rest of the game turned out to be pretty straightforward, though I
noted that it was deep in Gehennom (already having marked the VS and
getting ready to take out Vlad) before I found the only other
"reflection I saw.  I never saw a silver dragon.

On Astral I used !speed and the jumping boots, where I cleared all the
altars to find my own--and an Archon just outside the 3rd and final
altar dropped the only shield of reflection I saw all game.



